cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "AlpacaVision: near-duplicate leakage audit and alpaca detection benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, audit tools and results for an openly licensed detection benchmark of
  alpacas and other South American camelids assembled from public sources: 1461
  images from 517 distinct photographs (CC BY 4.0), audited for licence, label
  format, exact duplicates, near-duplicates and content. On a random image-level
  split, 82.3% of test images have a copy in training. A YOLOv11n detector reaches
  mAP@0.5 = 0.852 on the released split. A case study shows that a classifier
  trained on vision-language auto-labels of eye crops scores above chance while
  crop size alone predicts those labels better.
